# One face of a reel drum: a unit square, ready to be textured with a symbol.
#
# The drum is twelve of these, not one twelve sided mesh, because a symbol has
# to be chosen per facet at RUNTIME and pse::Renderer3D::draw_mesh carries one
# texture index for a whole mesh. Twelve instances of one quad is what lets a
# facet be repainted while it is out of sight, which is the trick that gives a
# twelve sided prism a reel strip of any length.
#
# Authored 1x1 and centred, so the game scales it to the facet size and the
# drum's radius follows: a twelve sided prism of radius R has facets
# 2*pi*R/12 tall, so a square facet means R = 12 * size / (2*pi).
#
# Wound for a -Z normal, which is the face pointing at the camera before any
# rotation. obj2cpp takes the cross the other way round (v x u), so this
# winding is the front facing one.
mtllib drum.mtl
o facet
v -0.500000 -0.500000 0.000000
v 0.500000 -0.500000 0.000000
v 0.500000 0.500000 0.000000
v -0.500000 0.500000 0.000000
vt 0.000000 0.000000
vt 1.000000 0.000000
vt 1.000000 1.000000
vt 0.000000 1.000000
usemtl face
f 1/1 2/2 3/3 4/4
